    "updated_at": "2021-06-01T17:08:45Z",
    "body": "Hi @Dentrax this is expected behaviour. There is no module called `disabled` so starship is pointing that out as an error. If you make the following changes to your config file this should fix it l\n\n```diff \n[kubernetes]\nformat = '[$symbol$context( \\($namespace\\))]($style) in '\ndisabled = true\nsymbol = '☸ '\n\n[kubernetes.context_aliases]\n\"dev.local.cluster.k8s\" = 'dev'\n\n- [disabled]\n- format = 'on [⛵ $context \\($namespace\\)](dimmed green) '\n- disabled = false\n- \n- [disabled.context_aliases]\n- \"dev.local.cluster.k8s\" = 'dev'\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
